! Setup

The plugin works with two services. Both store the comments in a public ~GitHub repository.

* [[giscus|https://giscus.app/]] (recommended) keeps the comments in ~GitHub Discussions and supports reactions, lazy loading and translations.
* [[utterances|https://utteranc.es/]] keeps the comments in ~GitHub Issues. Wikis configured before version 1.0.0 keep using it.

!! giscus

* Make sure the repo is public, otherwise your readers will not be able to view the discussions.
* Make sure the [[giscus app|https://github.com/apps/giscus]] is installed on the repo.
* Turn on the Discussions feature in the repo settings.
* Open [[giscus.app|https://giscus.app/]], enter the repo and pick a discussion category (''Announcements'' is recommended).
* Copy ''data-repo-id'', ''data-category'' and ''data-category-id'' from the generated script into the [[settings of the plugin|$:/plugins/breakzplatform/github-comments/settings/settings]], along with the repo and the website URL.
* Refresh your wiki.

!! utterances

* Make sure the repo is public, otherwise your readers will not be able to view the issues/comments.
* Make sure the [[utterances app|https://github.com/apps/utterances]] is installed on the repo, otherwise users will not be able to post comments.
* If your repo is a fork, navigate to its settings tab and confirm the issues feature is turned on.
* Fill out the repo and website URL in the [[settings of the plugin|$:/plugins/breakzplatform/github-comments/settings/settings]] and leave the giscus fields empty (or set the service to ''utterances'').
* Refresh your wiki.

